// Q-128 The strings of `class={if on { "a" } else { "b" }}` are not read, though those of `on ? "a" : "b"` are: a misspelt class passes `quillo check`
// mode: cli
// args: check Q-128-classes-in-an-if-are-not-read.qwe
// fixed-when: no style sheet has a rule for `.okk`
// From FEEDBACK16.md §Q-128 (found on b28e689).

css(".ok { color: red }")

fn a(on) = <p class={if on { "ok" } else { "okk" }}>1</p>
